# 2. File System Management

## History

The UNIX hierarchical file system was introduced in **1969**.

Linux inherited:

```
/
├── home
├── etc
├── var
├── usr
├── bin
├── opt
└── tmp
```

### Important Commands

```bash
ls
pwd
cd
mkdir
rmdir
cp
mv
rm
find
du
df
```

### File Permissions

```bash
chmod
chown
chgrp
```

Example

```
-rwxr-xr-x
```

